## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect true cross-project isolation with scalable tenant onboarding, plus governance controls across storage, analytics, and metadata systems.

## Key Concepts
- IAM conditions and per-tenant service accounts
- Tenant-specific data planes (GCS prefixes, BigQuery datasets)
- Private Service Connect and VPC Service Controls for restricted egress
- Data Catalog/Dataplex as a data governance layer
- Dataflow/Test hooks for ingestion, auditing, rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-config: per-tenant IAM condition binding (conceptual)
{
  "binding": {
    "members": ["serviceAccount:tenant-123@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com"],
    "role": "roles/bigquery.dataViewer",
    "condition": {
      "title": "Tenant-specific dataset access",
      "expression": "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/datasets/tenant_123_')"
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time ingestion basics, per-tenant routing, idempotence, and basic observability on GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming sources; Dataflow (Python) transforms
- BigQuery per-tenant tables with environmental isolation
- Idempotence via insertId; dead-letter queue handling
- Basic monitoring and dashboards for latency/cost

## Code Example
```javascript
class ValidateAndRoute {
  process(element) {
    const data = JSON.parse(element);
    if (!data.tenant_id || !data.timestamp || data.value == null) return;
    return [{ tenant: data.tenant_id, value: data.value }];
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test DLQ routing and failed-event replay?
- What metrics would you surface in a simple dashboard to catch data skew or lag?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design isolation-first, compliant, scalable SaaS on GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-Region Spanner per-tenant for isolation
- Pub/Sub + Dataflow routing
- Private access with VPC Service Controls + Private Service Connect
- Per-tenant analytics datasets, auditability, DR strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example IAM policy snippet (conceptual)
const policy = {
  bindings: [
    { role: 'roles/spanner.databaseUser', members: ['serviceAccount:ingest@example-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com'] }
  ]
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test data residency and audit trail completeness?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant Spanner databases vs. shared database with tenant_id column?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes multi-tenant data governance, isolation, and automation at scale in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant IAM and least privilege bindings
- VPC Service Controls and boundary design
- BigQuery, Pub/Sub, and Cloud Storage isolation patterns
- Automated onboarding/offboarding and cost controls
- End-to-end auditing with Cloud Audit Logs and Eventarc

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo example: build per-tenant IAM policy and apply
function buildTenantPolicy(tenantSA){
  return {
    bindings: [
      { role: 'roles/bigquery.dataViewer', members: [`serviceAccount:${tenantSA}`] },
      { role: 'roles/pubsub.subscriber', members: [`serviceAccount:${tenantSA}`] }
    ]
  };
}
// applyPolicy(projectId, tenantPolicy)
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce data residency and cross-tenant leakage detection without performance penalties?
- How would you test onboarding/offboarding and ensure no stale access remains?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a production-grade multi-tenant pipeline with strict data isolation, governance, and cost controls across GCP services, plus a robust testing and rollback strategy.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation with per-tenant Cloud Storage and per-tenant BigQuery datasets
- Dataflow pipeline correctness, idempotence, and scheduling
- IAM and IAM Conditions for least privilege
- Cross-region DR, data residency, and backup strategy
- Cost visibility with labels and budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
class ValidateAndEnrich {
  process(element) {
    if (!valid_schema(element)) return;
    const enriched = enrich(element);
    return enriched;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema changes across tenants without downtime?
- How do you enforce per-tenant security boundaries in a shared data lake?

